Implementing a text editor with multiple lists (multitextlist) in Angular involves several steps: setting up the environment, creating components for the text editor and list, and integrating them together. Below is a step-by-step guide to help you achieve this:

### Step 1: Set Up Your Project

First, ensure that your project has Angular installed. If not, install it using npm or yarn.

```bash
npm install @angular/cli --global
ng new multitexteditor-app
cd multitexteditor-app
```

### Step 2: Create Components

Create two main components: `TextEditor` and `Multilist`.

#### Text Editor Component (`text-editor.component.ts`)

```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-text-editor',
  templateUrl: './text-editor.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./text-editor.component.css']
})
export class TextEditorComponent {
  text = '';

  onChange(value: string) {
    this.text = value;
  }
}
```

#### Multilist Component (`multilist.component.ts`)

```typescript
import { Component, Input } from '@angular/core';
import { TextEditorComponent } from './text-editor/text-editor.component';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-multilist',
  templateUrl: './multilist.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./multilist.component.css'],
  providers: [TextEditorComponent]
})
export class MultilistComponent {
  @Input() texts: any[] = [];
}
```

### Step 3: Define Templates

#### Text Editor Template (`text-editor.component.html`)

```html
<input [(ngModel)]="text" type="text">
<button (click)="onChange()">Submit</button>
<p>{{ text }}</p>
```

#### Multilist Template (`multilist.component.html`)

```html
<div *ngFor="let item of texts; let i = index;">
  <input [(ngModel)]="item.text" type="text" #txt[i]="!i || null">
  <div>
    <label>{{ txt[i].text }}</label>
    <button (click)="removeItem(i)">Remove</button>
  </div>
</div>
```

### Step 4: Add Services if Needed

If you need services like communication between components, you might want to add some service declarations. However, for a simple setup, we don't strictly require services here.

### Step 5: Run the Application

Now, run your application:

```bash
ng serve
```

Open your browser at http://localhost:4200/ to see both components working together.

### Step 6: Integrate Multiple Lists

To integrate multiple lists into one component, you can use Angular's `*ngFor` directive inside a parent component template. Here’s an example:

#### Parent Component (`main-component.component.html`):

```html
<app-text-editor></app-text-editor>

<multilist 
  [texts]="texts"></multilist>
```

In your parent component file (`main-component.component.ts`), define the `texts` array:

```typescript
